# Silvian's chat window and Help button (Content/NPCs/Silvian/SilvianCounsel). Item names arrive with their icon
# already attached, and principle and temperament names arrive coloured. Numbered groups can grow: every entry from
# 0 up to the first gap is used.
SilvianCounsel: {
	HelpButton: Help

	# His chat window. {0} is the player's name. Chat is always in the draw; the others join it while they apply.
	Chat: {
		0: How goes it, {0}? Garden's comin' along nicely, if I do say so myself.
		1: Dayblooms want the sun, and blinkroots want the dark and the damp. Plants are a lot like people that way. Hehe.
		2: Got a question? Hold it up and hit Help. I'm no Guide, but I know my herbs.
		3: Bring me anything strange you dig up out there. I'll tell ya whether it's worth boilin'.
		4: My uncle could name a potion just by the smell of it. Me, I still gotta read the label.
		5: Salt line's holdin'. Saw a blue slime sniff at it this mornin' and turn right back around. Best thing I've seen all week.
		6: Folks think gardenin's quiet work. Ain't nothin' quiet about a bunny in your seed beds at three in the mornin'.
		7: I talk to the plants. Uncle J swore it helps. Can't say it does much for them, but it sure does somethin' for me.
		8: You eat yet, {0}? You look like you've been livin' off whatever mushrooms you found on the ground. Don't do that, by the way.
		9: Uncle J labeled his bottles in writin' so small you needed a lens to read it. Took me a whole summer to find the cough syrup.
		10: If you ever see a slime wearin' a crown, you run. Don't ask me how I know.
		11: Got a roof, a kettle and a garden. Man don't need much more than that. ...Maybe a second kettle.
		12: Don't mind the dirt on the floor. Or my boots. Or, well, most things 'round here.
		13: Hand me a seed and I'll tell ya where it wants to grow. Hand me a bottle and I'll tell ya what Uncle J would've done with it. Hand me a sword and I'll just sorta look at it.
	}

	# After dusk.
	ChatNight: {
		0: Bit late to be wanderin' about, {0}. Zombies ain't known for their manners.
		1: Blinkroots are glowin' tonight. Pretty, ain't it? Uncle J called 'em the garden's night-lights.
		2: Can't sleep either, huh? I've been countin' seeds instead of sheep. Up to four hundred and twelve.
		3: Keep your voice down. Moonglow's openin' up and I don't wanna spook it.
	}

	# While it rains.
	ChatRain: {
		0: Now this is my kinda weather. Garden gets a drink and I don't haul a single bucket.
		1: Wipe your feet, would ya? Mud's for the moonglow, not my floor.
		2: Slimes love the rain. Reckon I'll be up all night watchin' the beds again.
	}

	# Once he has given the player his uncle's almanac.
	ChatAlmanac: {
		0: How's Uncle J's almanac treatin' ya? Don't go dog-earin' the pages. ...Alright, he dog-eared 'em too.
		1: Filled in any of those blank pages yet? He'd be tickled pink to see somebody else's writin' in there.
		2: Caught myself reachin' for the almanac on the shelf this mornin'. Forgot it's yours now. Habit, I guess.
	}

	# Help with nothing alchemical in hand, one per press, in order. Each session starts again from the top.
	Lessons: {
		0: Curious about somethin'? Pick it up on your cursor, or just hold it, and hit Help again. I'll tell ya what I know.
		1: First thing you'll need is an alchemy station. Uncle J knocked his together from a cookin' pot, a bottle and a bit of wood.
		2: Every brew starts with a solvent. That's your base, plain bottled water most of the time. It goes in the station's big slot, and everything else gets dissolved into it.
		3: Solutes are what you dissolve: herbs, ores, fish, all sorts. They go in the little slots. Most of 'em lean toward a principle, and the principle's what decides what your brew does.
		4: Reagents are solutes that don't lean any which way. Salts, acids, powders. They won't make a brew on their own, but they sure change one.
		5: What comes out the other end's a solution. Drink it, or set it back in the big slot and build on it.
		6: There's seven principles: Vital, Specular, Martial, Brisk, Fortune, Harmony and Bane. Each one's got its metal. Gold's Vital, iron's Martial, and so on.
		7: Temperaments are how a thing behaves: acidic or alkaline, volatile or kinetic, catalytic or inert. Mix opposites and they cancel each other out.
		8: Stack more of a solute in its slot and the brew comes out stronger, up to five stars. Costs you more leaves and stones though, mind.
		9: Brew somethin' new and it's written down for good. Found a potion you don't know how to make? Show it to me and I'll point ya the right way.
	}

	# Help with something on the cursor he can't speak to. {0} is the item.
	NotAlchemical: "{0}? Can't say that's much use to an alchemist. Show me a herb, an ore, a bottle, somethin' like that."
	# Help with the almanac itself.
	AboutAlmanac: Uncle J's almanac! Treat it kindly, now. And label your bottles, like he says.

	# What the item is, by the part it plays at the station. {0} is the item.
	Role: {
		Solvent: "{0}? That's a solvent: a base you pour in first, and everything else gets dissolved into it."
		Solute: "{0}? That's a solute. Goes in the station's little slots, to be dissolved into a solvent."
		Reagent: "{0}? That's a reagent. Doesn't lean any which way on its own, but it changes what the rest of a brew does."
		Solution: "{0}? That's a finished solution. Drink it, or set it back in the station's big slot to build on it."
		Other: "{0}? Uncle J's got a page on that one."
	}

	# What it leans toward and how it behaves. {0} its principles, {1} its temperaments and traits.
	Nature: {
		Both: It leans {0}, and the almanac marks it {1}.
		Principle: It leans {0}.
		Temperament: The almanac marks it {1}.
	}

	# Silvian quoting his uncle's almanac. {0} is the item's entry under Almanac.FlavorText.
	Quote: Uncle J's book says: "{0}"
	# How to make it, once it has been brewed in this world. {0} the solvent, {1} what goes in.
	Known: This one's been brewed around here before. Simplest way I know: {0} with {1}.
	# How to make it, before it has been brewed. Each ask gives the next hint; the last never names everything.
	Unbrewed: Nobody's brewed one of these around here yet, so here's a nudge.
	# {0} the solvent, {1} how many things go in.
	Hint1: Start from {0} and stir in {1} {^1:thing;things}.
	# {0} what goes in, each told only by what it leans toward.
	Hint2: What you stir in is {0}.
	# {0} one of the things that go in.
	Hint3: One of 'em's {0}. The rest you can work out yourself.
	HintMore: Ask me again if you're still stuck.
	HintsDone: That's all you're gettin' outta me. Secrets are earned, not handed over. Uncle J's words, not mine.
	NoRecipe: Can't say I know how that one's made. Some things you find, not brew.
	# What it goes into. {0} the brews already found, {1} how many are still to find.
	UsesKnown: It's already gone into {0}.
	UsesMore: There's {1} more {^1:brew;brews} it goes into that nobody's found yet.
	UsesUnknown: It goes into {1} {^1:brew;brews}, and nobody's found a one of 'em yet.
	# One ingredient told without naming it. {0} what it leans toward, else how it behaves.
	Something: somethin' {0}
	SomethingLiquid: another liquid
	SomethingPlain: somethin' plain
	# One ingredient accepted from a group, told by one member. {0} that member.
	OrTheLike: "{0} or the like"
	# One ingredient needed above one star. {0} the ingredient, {1} its stars.
	AtPotency: "{0} at {1} stars"
	# Lists. {0} and {1} are the items either side; AndMore ends a list cut short, {0} being how many were left off.
	And: "{0} and {1}"
	Comma: "{0}, {1}"
	AndMore: "{0} more"

	Principles: {
		Vital: Vital
		Specular: Specular
		Martial: Martial
		Brisk: Brisk
		Fortune: Fortune
		Harmony: Harmony
		Bane: Bane
	}
}
